  "sourceUrl": "https://resource.fs.com/mall/doc/20221114163118tn7bta.pdf",
  "notes": "Stated configuration, not a fixed chassis figure: the NC8200-4TD ships unloaded with 4 line-card slots, so the port list is 4x NC8200-24BC (24x 25G SFP28 + 2x 100G QSFP28 per card). A different fill is a different box - 4x NC8200-8C is 32x 100G, 4x NC8200-16Q is 64x 40G, and a mixed fill is anywhere in between - and needs its own spec rather than a reuse of this one.\n\nPort names follow FSOS: 25G ports are TFGigabitEthernet <slot>/<port> and 100G cages are HundredGigabitEthernet <slot>/<port>, with the slot being the line-card bay 1-4 (the CLI guide's line-card example is 'slot 3' on a 4-slot frame). The datasheet numbers the 24BC's SFP28 cages 1-24 and does not number its two QSFP28 cages, so those are modelled as the card's ports 1-2 of the 100G class; the cages' rates (40G/100G, or 4x 10G/4x 25G broken out) are from the datasheet's line-card note.\n\nSwitching capacity is where the two FS sources disagree and the datasheet wins: the NC8200 series datasheet (Table 5) gives 6.4 Tbps and 4.76 Bpps for this chassis, while the fs.com product page 110482 prints 3.2 Tbps. 6.4 Tbps is the duplex aggregate, 3.2 Tbps per direction - which is exactly what 96x 25G + 8x 100G sums to - so fabric.capacityMbps is 3,200,000 and a full 4x NC8200-24BC load is line-rate, not oversubscribed. The figure is recorded per direction because the fabric audit compares it with the sum of the ports, and a duplex 6,400,000 would have claimed the box was half-empty.\n\nThe headline '128x 10G/25G' density in the product overview is not a fourth card type: it is this fill with the eight QSFP28 cages broken out to 4x 25G, which is why the chassis keeps 32x 100G of cage capacity but only 3.2 Tbps of fabric.\n\nManagement and console: the datasheet lists 1 management port, 1 console port (RS-232 levels on a standard RJ45) and 1 Mini-USB B console port, and states no rate for the management port, so only the RJ-45 console is modelled; the Mini-USB B socket is the same console by another connector and the management NIC is out-of-band.\n\nNo PoE anywhere in the datasheet: power is 2x 1+1 hot-swap AC (800 W modules), 600 W max consumption, so no poe-pse and no budget. Stacking is 2 members with 48 VSL links on the 24BC card, and NC8200-24BC stacks only with other 24BC cards. VXLAN-EVPN, MLAG, BGP4+, OSPFv2/v3, IS-IS, PFC/ECN and RoCEv2 are software features and are not modelled as port capabilities."
